// WHAT WAS DELIBERATELY NOT TAUGHT, collected for the reviewer. Each is a refusal with a reason,
// and lesson 23 teaches the list to the learner rather than hiding it in a comment:
//   - Any step-by-step repair procedure, on any system. The public record does not carry it and
//     content/construction/ may not be used. Gate A4 plus B4.
//   - Any method for disturbing lead paint. The course teaches the prohibited practices and the
//     containment distances as things to CHECK a firm against, never as instructions.
//   - Any asbestos identification, sampling or removal method. EPA says sampling yourself is not
//     recommended and that improper removal may increase exposure.
//   - Any mould remediation method beyond EPA's own published householder threshold.
//   - Any radon mitigation method. EPA says it requires technical knowledge and special skills.
//   - Any gas work at all. The single gas instruction in the course is CPSC's, and it is to leave.
//   - Any service-panel work. CPSC names a qualified electrician three separate times.
//   - Any structural or roof work.
//   - Any statement that a named trade is licensed in a named place, or that a named job needs a
//     permit in a named place. Only federal sources plus 675 IAC 14-4.4-1 were read.
//   - Any line of model code text. Section numbers are cited as addresses only.
//   - Any credential, implied or stated. Lesson 19 exists so that "I ran the checklist" is never
//     mistaken for "the house was inspected".
